; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Compound Interest
; CATEGORY: Mathematics
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     money, percentages, growth, charts, loops
; SUMMARY:  Compares simple and compound interest year by year with a table and a side-by-side bar chart.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   You put 100 dollars in a bank that pays 10 percent a year.
;   With simple interest you get 10 dollars every year, always the
;   same. With compound interest you earn interest on your interest
;   too, so each year's gift is a little bigger than the last. The
;   chart shows both: grey bars for simple, green bars for compound.
;   Watch the green bars pull away.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change :start, :rate and :years at the top.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * percentages: multiplying by 1 + rate/100 adds rate percent
;   * a variable that is updated every time around a loop
;   * the difference between adding the same amount and multiplying
;   * ROUND and FORM to show money with two decimal places
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * The "rule of 72": at 10 percent, money doubles in about
;     72 / 10 = 7.2 years. Find the doubling year in the table.
;   * Try a rate of 5 or 20. Does the rule of 72 still work?
;   * Make :years 30 and :barscale smaller so the bars fit.
; ============================================================

make "start 100
make "rate 10
make "years 20
; how many screen steps tall one dollar is
make "barscale 0.64

to money :x
  output word "$ form :x 0 2
end

; One bar. Its bottom-left corner is at (x, -230).
to bar :x :width :amount :color
  penup setxy :x -230 setheading 0
  filled :color [
    forward :amount * :barscale right 90
    forward :width right 90
    forward :amount * :barscale right 90
    forward :width right 90
  ]
end

to growth
  localmake "simple :start
  localmake "compound :start
  print "|year     simple     compound|
  for [y 1 :years] [
    ; simple: always the same 10 percent of the STARTING money
    make "simple :simple + :start * :rate / 100
    ; compound: 10 percent of whatever is in the bank NOW
    make "compound :compound * (1 + :rate / 100)
    print (sentence form :y 4 0 form :simple 11 2 form :compound 12 2)
    localmake "x -360 + (:y - 1) * 36
    bar :x 15 :simple [170 170 170]
    bar :x + 15 15 :compound [40 160 90]
    if 0 = remainder :y 5 [
      penup setxy :x + 6 -250 setpencolor [60 60 60] setlabelheight 12 label :y
    ]
  ]
  print "
  print (sentence [After] :years [years, simple interest gives] money :simple)
  print (sentence [and compound interest gives] money :compound)
  penup setlabelheight 16 setpencolor [40 160 90]
  setxy -360 250 label (sentence [compound:] money :compound)
  setpencolor [120 120 120]
  setxy -360 225 label (sentence [simple:] money :simple)
end

clearscreen hideturtle
growth
penup setxy -370 -230 setheading 90 setpencolor "black setpensize 2
pendown forward 740
penup setxy -40 -275 setlabelheight 14 label [years]
setxy 40 250 setlabelheight 18
label (sentence money :start [at] word :rate "% [a year])
